id: pm-76fkpp
title: Provide an audited repair and severity-migration contract for legacy invalid provenance
description: "GH-998 documents 1,255 immutable events written by older pm-cli versions with CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION captured as role=1. The capture bug and advisory disposition are closed, but no supported repair exists and severity changed across releases. Add a privacy-safe dry-run plan and audited rewrite/disposition path, plus an explicit compatibility policy for validation severity changes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: compatibility,history,provenance,recovery
created_at: "2026-08-13T22:04:10.579Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:39.144Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:38.233Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:38.233Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: A supported command inventories and dry-runs invalid legacy provenance repairs without exposing raw sensitive values; an authorized apply path preserves hash-chain and workspace replay integrity with an immutable audit receipt; health remediation names the exact command; validation severity cannot become blocking before compatible repair exists and is announced; GH-998 is linked in evidence
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Operators can inventory, dry-run, and normalize invalid legacy provenance without exposing raw provenance values or breaking history integrity."
actual_result: "SDK, CLI, and MCP contracts now provide aggregate-only provenance census and normalization receipts; apply mode rewrites invalid observations and reanchors the chain."
